-- title:
--   Inertia fixing μₚ and (1+p)^{1/p} acts residually trivially
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative local ring, $p$ a prime with $p$ lying in the maximal ideal of $B$, and write $G$ for the group of $\mathbb{Q}_p$-algebra automorphisms of `PadicAlgCl p`. Given functions $x,z\colon G\to B^{\times}$ and $y\colon G\to B$, assume: $z\tau=1$ for every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of the valuation subring [`padicIntegers p`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L20) of `PadicAlgCl p` over $\mathbb{Q}_p$ (that is, the image in $G$ of the inertia subgroup inside the decomposition subgroup); and for all $g\in G$ and all $n,a\in\mathbb{N}$, if $g\mu=\mu^{a}$ for every $\mu$ with $\mu^{p^{n}}=1$, then $x g\cdot z g-a$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^{n}$. Let $\eta\in B$ be a unit and $\zeta\in$ `PadicAlgCl p` a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Assume further that for every additive map $\Lambda$ from the residue field of $B$ to $\mathbb{Z}/p$ there are units $a\in\mathbb{Q}_p^{\times}$ and $\alpha$ of `PadicAlgCl p` with $a=\alpha^{p}$, with $g\alpha=\zeta^{\,\Lambda(\overline{\eta\, y g\,(z g)^{-1}})}\alpha$ for all $g\in G$ (the exponent being the natural-number representative of the value of $\Lambda$ on the residue class), and with $p\mid v_p(a)$; and that every nonzero $c\in\mathbb{Q}_p$ with $p\mid v_p(c)$ can be written $c=(1+p)^{r}w^{p}$ with $r\in\mathbb{N}$, $w\in\mathbb{Q}_p$. Then there exists $\beta\in$ `PadicAlgCl p` with $\beta^{p}=1+p$ such that every $\tau$ in that inertia subgroup which fixes all $p$-th roots of unity and fixes $\beta$ satisfies $x\tau-1\in\mathfrak{m}_B$, $y\tau\in\mathfrak{m}_B$ and $z\tau=1$.
--
--   This is the local step which converts a Kummer-theoretic hypothesis on the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-valuations of the relevant Kummer elements into residual triviality, on the subgroup of inertia fixing $\mu_p$ and one $p$-th root of $1+p$, of the triple $(x,y,z)$ recording a deformation of a local representation. It is used in the derivation of [`GaloisRepAdic.exists_root_one_add_prime_inertia_sub_mem_of_quotientScalar_sq_sub_one_mem_span_socle`](thm.html#GaloisRepAdic.exists_root_one_add_prime_inertia_sub_mem_of_quotientScalar_sq_sub_one_mem_span_socle).
